  "summary": "VirusTotal's Internet Scanning data exposes per-port service banners, products/versions, CPEs and SSH/RDP fingerprints for the public IPv4 space, enabling pivots on rare host keys, certificate subjects and service stacks. The post shows the technique unmasking a NOX/BOMBAY Stealer operator login panel on 5.175.221.206:8443 hosted on a Windows Server 2022 host with SMB/RDP exposed, and hunting FTP-banner dead drop resolvers that pipe a banner-embedded 'ftp <ip>|powershell' command into a shell. Detection value lies in the service banners, panel strings and multi-port host signatures rather than in raw open ports.",
